<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Are electric vehicles really bad for the environment?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b988ab5adc824171798d366688b8887ce6f4790832db83e2faff37e0b46744</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-electric-vehicles-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336--2b5b564fe6cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-electric-vehicles-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some German politicians are calling for a delay to the EU plan to phase out gas-powered vehicles, saying cars must be judged on the entire carbon footprint. But the full picture still says EVs are more climate friendly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ECB raises interest rates to fight off inflation jump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c78f593ab53bd6775a33cb9e179d87165d812ad787a63c5f23e758099528321</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ecb-raises-interest-rates-to-fight-off-inflation-jump/a-79215209--f35c3a697cd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ecb-raises-interest-rates-to-fight-off-inflation-jump/a-79215209?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Central Bank raised borrowing costs and warned that inflation could remain high for an extended period. Energy markets and geopolitical tensions are still major concerns.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Weidel face off after AfD state win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4cd7afb758593197dffdbe05f1ee8e422bfaec65efe27ff676acd8f475977dae</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246--7057d0c40f30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alice Weidel and Friedrich Merz traded barbs in the Bundestag days after the AfD's victory in Saxony-Anhalt put new pressure on the German chancellor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sets its sights on Russia's shadow fleet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7262a66ad3342c69f6ea64666b5c0d39b823bda6822f5b8e6ec8679b6f4f4a4</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123--786b113b7d97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government wants to follow other EU countries and take more decisive action against Russia's shadow fleet, accusing it of helping Moscow evade sanctions and carry out acts of sabotage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Cyberattack in Berlin: 1.4 million files on the dark web</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5e7e5d793a111786538d3e759d31d3828ba310c8005b0d39524a77e7bb04a50</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyberattack-in-berlin-1-4-million-files-on-the-dark-web/a-79220829--b03a66e17cd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyberattack-in-berlin-1-4-million-files-on-the-dark-web/a-79220829?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shortly before Berlin's state parliamentary election, the hacker group Rhysida stole data, tried to extort the Berlin Senate and published the data on the dark web after their attempt failed.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2544e775e5f4750f7697ddc74e9c7596a55ce94bcac64ec4100d693883201f</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:11:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-attacks/a-79202918--9a576424ceac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg by the so-called Hamburg cell. A look back at a day that reshaped Germany's approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-10T19:10:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
